# Using the `aiven-docs` MCP server

The `aiven-docs` MCP server indexes the Aiven documentation
(github.com/aiven/devportal). Ground answers about Aiven in it instead of memory.

- Call `search` before answering. Put exact identifiers in the query when you know
  them (`max_connections`, `kafka.auto_create_topics_enable`, `avn service create`).
- Answer only from the returned `content`. Cite the `web_url` (or `source_uri`) of
  every chunk you used, as a Markdown link.
- If the results do not contain the answer, search again once or twice with
  different wording or a narrower `uri_prefix`, e.g.
  `github.com/aiven/devportal/docs/products/postgresql/`.
- If it is still not there, say the docs do not cover it. Do not invent parameters,
  limits or CLI flags.
- Use `list_sources` to check what is indexed. Only call `ingest` or
  `delete_source` when the user asks for it.
